WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:02.468
♪ (UPBEAT JAZZ MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.503
TARAJI P. HENSON:
 I brush my teeth.

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:05.871
 I smile.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.541
But there is always this frown.

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:13.346
 I think I'll run away
 with the ants...

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.116
 and live on Mars.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.918
♪ (MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.320
 And I'm fortunate
 because I'm a poet,

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:23.055
 and poets are allowed
 to be hopeful.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:27.459
I used to dream radical dreams
of blowing everyone away

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:31.030
with my perceptive powers
of correct analysis.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.433
 I don't remember
 a lot of things.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.837
 But a lot of things
 that I don't remember,

00:00:37.903 --> 00:00:39.472
I don't choose to remember.

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:42.842
 Childhood remembrances
 are always a drag

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:44.544
 if you're Black.

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:49.315
I remember what's important,
 and I make up the rest.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.184
That's what storytelling's
 all about.

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:56.889
 I even used to think
I'd be the one to stop the riots

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:58.791
 and negotiate the peace.

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:00.926
STUDENT: Would you ever say
that some of your poems

00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:03.395
were inspired by stress
or hate?

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:07.299
STUDENT 2: Were you ever
bullied by your skin color
when you were younger?

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.769
STUDENT 3: Have you ever had,
like, a breakdown,

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.037
where you couldn't take
it anymore,

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.406
where you just couldn't do it?

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:18.277
But there has to be a way
to do what we do and survive.

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:21.114
Our ancestors taught us
how to do that.

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:24.517
NIKKI: The one thing
 that I did know

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:27.920
is whatever life would be,
I knew I had to create myself.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:30.456
To successfully go to Mars
 and back,

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:32.292
 you will need a song.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.361
 And maybe a six pack,

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:38.231
so if there is life on Mars,
 you can share.

00:01:39.631 --> 00:01:41.934
Popcorn for the celebration
 when you land,

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:44.204
 while you wait on
your land legs to kick in.

00:01:45.671 --> 00:01:49.041
 And as you climb down
the ladder from your spaceship

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:51.110
 to the Martian surface,
 look to your left,

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:54.547
 and there you'll see
 a smiling community

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:59.285
quilting a black-eyed pea,
watching you descend.

00:01:59.585 --> 00:02:00.487
(CHUCKLES)

